# Two-Axis Code Review Evidence: L3 Tools Layer and L4 Desktop Environment Hosts
File: openOODA/audits/nextgen/axis/l3_l4_evidence.oot

Provenance: Batch 8 two-axis review. Part 2 of 2 (see `l3_l4_findings.oot` for the findings).

Scope: 8 canonical `openOODA-DE` repositories and 8 consolidated `openOODA-tools` hosts, all at
`origin/master`.

Redaction note: fleet host names and tailnet addresses are written as generic placeholders.

## 1. The gate before the repairs

The gate of the three hosts that answered below the full quorum:

```
oocap          hat=black ... standards_findings=8 spec_findings=0 ... status=REFUSAL
oorepl         hat=black ... standards_findings=9 spec_findings=0 ... status=REFUSAL
oosemanticdiff hat=black ... standards_findings=8 spec_findings=0 ... status=REFUSAL
cycle=FAIL exit=2 verdict=fail
```

The quorum of the three hosts was `quorum_mask=104`: the white hat and the yellow hat were missing.
The white hat counts the shape law of rules.oot 1.8 and the black hat counts the same law. The
violations were:

```
oocap/main.oo                 LONGFN(84)   84 lines of code against the bound of 64
oocap/ipc/json_field.oo       DEEP(8)      eight nested blocks against the bound of four
oorepl/core/engine.oo         LONG_LINE(147)
oosemanticdiff/core/engine.oo LONG_LINE(147)
```

The other five tools hosts and the eight DE hosts answered with the full quorum at the start of the
batch.

