## 3. The build, the verification and the tests

One line per tools host. The build, the verification and the tests each answer with the exit code 0
and the test suite prints `ALL TESTS PASSED`.

```
oocap          build=0 verify=0 test=0  ALL TESTS PASSED
oorepl         build=0 verify=0 test=0  ALL TESTS PASSED
oosemanticdiff build=0 verify=0 test=0  ALL TESTS PASSED
oocsplit       build=0 verify=0 test=0  ALL TESTS PASSED
oobinview      build=0 verify=0 test=0  ALL TESTS PASSED
oohexdump      build=0 verify=0 test=0  ALL TESTS PASSED
oostrdiff      build=0 verify=0 test=0  ALL TESTS PASSED
oosqlite       build=0 verify=0 test=0  ALL TESTS PASSED
```

The compiler is always named on the command line, because the Makefiles export their own value and
silently override the ambient one:

```
OODA_COMPILER=/Projects/openOODA-core/oodac/bin/oodac make build
OODA_COMPILER=/Projects/openOODA-core/oodac/bin/oodac make verify
OODA_COMPILER=/Projects/openOODA-core/oodac/bin/oodac make test
```

Every page of every tools host passes the compiler check:

```
oorepl: 0 page check failures
oosemanticdiff: 0 page check failures
oosqlite: 0 page check failures
oostrdiff: 0 page check failures
oocsplit: 0 page check failures
```

The size lint answers with the exit code 0 for all eight hosts.

## 4. The refusal of the unknown options

Every host answers an unknown option, a persona flag, a persona flag with a value and a persona
list with the exit code 2. The line holds the four exit codes in that order.

```
oocap          2 2 2 2
oorepl         2 2 2 2
oosemanticdiff 2 2 2 2
oocsplit       2 2 2 2
oobinview      2 2 2 2
oohexdump      2 2 2 2
oostrdiff      2 2 2 2
oosqlite       2 2 2 2
```

The persona table of `oostrdiff` answers with the exit code 2 as well:

```
oostrdiff --personas -> 2
```

## 5. The native engine of `oohexdump`

The engine is compared with the upstream tool over eight formats, four address radixes and seven
files, which is 224 runs. Every run holds the standard output and the exit code of the upstream
tool:

```
224/224 identical
```

The gate of the repository holds the engine against the upstream tool as well:

```
PARITY ./dist/oohexdump against od match=11 differ=1 skip=0 fail=0
```

The eleven match cases are the formats `x1z x1 x2 o2 u2 d2 a c`, the address radixes `x d o`, the
read window `-N 4`, the skip `-j 2` and the width `--width=8`. The one differ case is the file that
is not there: the exit code is the same and the text of the answer is its own, because the language
has no lowering for the error stream.

The engine answers under the empty path, and the answer is the answer of the upstream tool:

```
$ PATH=/nonexistent ./dist/oohexdump -A x -t x1z bin.bin
000000 00 01 02 03 c8 ff 0a 20 09 07 30 31 32 00 00 00  >....... ..012...<
000010 00                                               >.<
000011

$ od -A x -t x1z bin.bin
000000 00 01 02 03 c8 ff 0a 20 09 07 30 31 32 00 00 00  >....... ..012...<
000010 00                                               >.<
000011
```

Before the repair the same command answered:

```
$ PATH=/nonexistent ./dist/oohexdump bin.bin
ERR upstream od failed
```

## 6. The commits

Seven repositories carry a commit of this batch. `oobinview` answered with the full quorum at the
start of the batch and needed no change.

```
openOODA-tools/oocap          f1f742b  fix(shape): one statement per line and the oohat quorum at 255
openOODA-tools/oorepl         f1915c5  fix(cli): refuse the options the CLI does not answer with exit 2
openOODA-tools/oosemanticdiff 59cac6d  fix(cli): refuse the options the CLI does not answer with exit 2
openOODA-tools/oocsplit       2d0a43b  fix(cli): an unknown option is refused with exit 2
openOODA-tools/oohexdump      1d0aa90  feat(od): the native engine replaces the host od
openOODA-tools/oostrdiff      be41a07  fix(cli): drop the persona table and refuse the options the CLI does not answer
openOODA-tools/oosqlite       a950381  fix(cli): drop the persona flag and refuse the options the CLI does not answer
```

Every commit was verified on the host of the repository after the push, and the head of every
repository was compared with the head of the branch on the host.

## 7. The environment

The host is shared and heavily oversubscribed, and the compiler allocates about 1.1 GB for every
process that emits the intermediate form. The builds of this batch were therefore run one
repository at a time. The scratch space of the review was written outside the temporary partition,
which held 79 percent of its capacity.

The reviews were made in clean clones of `origin/master`, because the live trees of the tools
hosts carry the uncommitted work of a concurrent session. The state of those trees at the end of
the batch was left untouched.
